        "TECHNIQUE 2: SCAMPER",
        "What is SCAMPER?",
        "SCAMPER is a creative thinking checklist that helps you look at problems from different angles. It's an acronym representing seven different ways to modify existing ideas or products.",
        "Simple Explanation:",
        "Imagine you have a bicycle and want to improve it. SCAMPER gives you 7 different questions to ask: Can you replace parts? Combine it with something? Make it bigger/smaller? And so on!",
        "The SCAMPER Framework",
        "S – SUBSTITUTE",
        "Question: What can you replace or swap?",
        "Think about:",
        "Materials (replace plastic with bamboo)",
        "Processes (replace manual with automatic)",
        "People (replace expert with AI)",
        "Ingredients (replace sugar with honey)",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Replace metal frame with flexible plastic → Unbreakable umbrella",
        "Replace fabric with transparent material → See-through umbrella",
        "Replace handle with phone holder → Hands-free umbrella",
        "C – COMBINE",
        "Question: What can you bring together or merge?",
        "Think about:",
        "Combining products (phone + camera)",
        "Combining features (lamp + speaker)",
        "Combining services (gym + cafe)",
        "Combining ideas from different fields",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Umbrella + flashlight → Night visibility",
        "Umbrella + solar panel → Charges phone",
        "Umbrella + bag → Converts into backpack when folded",
        "A – ADAPT",
        "Question: What else is like this? What can you copy or adjust?",
        "Think about:",
        "Borrowing ideas from other industries",
        "Learning from nature (biomimicry)",
        "Adapting historical solutions",
        "Adjusting for different contexts",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Adapt tent mechanism → Pop-up automatic umbrella",
        "Adapt parachute design → Ultra-strong, wind-resistant",
        "Adapt flower petals → Self-cleaning surface",
        "M – MODIFY/MAGNIFY/MINIFY",
        "Question: What can you change, make bigger, or make smaller?",
        "Modify: Change shape, color, sound, meaning",
        "Magnify: Make larger, stronger, longer, more frequent",
        "Minify: Make smaller, lighter, shorter, less frequent",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Modify:",
        "Change shape → Square umbrella (covers more)",
        "Change color → UV-reactive (changes color in sun)",
        "Magnify:",
        "Make bigger → Family-size umbrella for 4 people",
        "Make stronger → Withstands hurricane-force winds",
        "Minify:",
        "Make smaller → Pocket-size umbrella fits in wallet",
        "Make lighter → Ultra-light carbon fiber (100 grams)",
        "P – PUT TO OTHER USES",
        "Question: What else can this be used for?",
        "Think about:",
        "Alternative purposes",
        "New markets/users",
        "Different contexts",
        "Repurposing waste",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Use as walking stick when closed",
        "Use as beach sun shade",
        "Use as weapon for self-defense",
        "Use as collection device for rainwater",
        "E – ELIMINATE",
        "Question: What can you remove or simplify?",
        "Think about:",
        "Unnecessary features",
        "Extra steps in process",
        "Redundant components",
        "Complexity that confuses users",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Remove handle → Wear like a hat",
        "Remove ribs → Use tension fabric (lighter)",
        "Remove button → Opens by gesture",
        "Remove entire umbrella → Develop water-repelling jacket instead!",
        "R – REVERSE/REARRANGE",
        "Question: What if you did it backwards or changed the sequence?",
        "Reverse: Do opposite, turn upside down, role reversal",
        "Rearrange: Change order, swap components, different layout",
        "Example – Improving Umbrella:",
        "Reverse:",
        "Inside-out design → Wet side folds inward (doesn't drip)",
        "Open downward → Catches rainwater for gardening",
        "User stays dry → Umbrella protects bags/packages instead",
        "Rearrange:",
        "Handle at top → Umbrella stands independently",
        "Multiple canopies → Modular umbrella system",
