        "✅ Shows where users get stuck",
        "✅ Provides actionable insights for improvement",
        "✅ Relatively quick and inexpensive",
        "Limitations:",
        "❌ Artificial environment (not real-world usage)",
        "❌ Observer effect (users act differently when watched)",
        "❌ Limited sample size",
        "❌ Can't test long-term usage patterns",
        "METHOD 2: A/B TESTING (Split Testing)",
        "What is A/B Testing?",
        "Definition:",
        "Showing two different versions (A and B) to different users and measuring which performs better statistically.",
        "Simple Explanation:",
        "You have two versions of your design. Show Version A to 50 people and Version B to another 50 people. Whichever version gets better results wins!",
        "How A/B Testing Works",
        "Step 1: Choose What to Test",
        "Select one specific element to compare.",
        "Examples:",
